+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling Stays Out
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The 2026-08-08 non-goal ADR confirmed NG-5 as a deliberate product decision. It recorded that any narrowing would require its own non-goal ADR. The owner has now made that narrowing decision (2026-08-27): a booked visit should be correctable so a mis-entered date or description can be fixed. Cancelling it should still never be allowed.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** A booked visit stays immutable. Rejected: the owner wants forward correction of a mistaken date or description, which the create-and-update pattern elsewhere in the sample already teaches for owners and pets.
+2. **Narrow NG-5 to open both correction and cancellation.** Rejected: cancelling a booked visit removes a record, which is the deletion pattern NG-4 already declines; opening it would reopen a settled boundary.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to correction only** (chosen). Date and description become correctable; cancellation stays out.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-5 is narrowed. Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope as REQ-VIS-003. A correction is validated as a booking is and updates the existing visit in place, adding no new visit. Cancelling a booked visit remains out of scope — removing a booking is the deletion pattern NG-4 declines.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-5 now reads as "Cancelling a visit once booked"; the correction capability moves into the Requirements section as REQ-VIS-003.
+- The sample gains a visit-correction flow that mirrors the owner and pet update flows, so no new lifecycle state is introduced.
+- A visible entry point to the correction from the owner's record is not part of this decision and is left as an open question.
+- Cancelling a booked visit stays declined; reopening it would require its own recorded owner decision.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row and preamble.
+- [PRD Visits / REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the in-scope correction capability.
+- Narrows the NG-5 half of [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md).
